   "text": {
    "L1": "A fraction of a measure depends on the whole measure.",
    "L2": "A kilo is 1000 grams, so we divide it into four equal parts for one quarter.",
    "L3": "One quarter kilo is 1000 shared into 4, which is 250 grams.",
    "L4": "Three quarters means 3 equal parts, not 3 pieces of any size.",
    "L5": "Three times 250 grams is 750 grams, so three-quarter kilo is 750 grams.",
    "L6": "The same idea works for other measures: half a litre is 500 millilitres, and half a metre is 50 centimetres.",
    "L7": "Now check yourself: a quarter kilo is how many grams?"
   },
